<section class="am-extra-content section-padding"><div class="container"><header class="am-extra-lead wow fadeInUp"><span>Build knowledge, faith, and character</span><h2>Islamic Studies</h2><p>Build a foundation in faith, worship, moral values and Islamic principles with lessons tailored to the learner age and level.</p><p>At Al-Asim Quran, our Islamic Studies program is designed to help students gain a strong foundation in the essential teachings of Islam. This course aims to develop a deep understanding of faith, worship, moral values, and Islamic principles that guide everyday life.</p></header>

<div class="row g-4 am-extra-grid">
<div class="col-lg-6"><article class="am-extra-card wow fadeInUp" data-wow-delay="0.00s"><span class="am-extra-index">01</span><h2>What You Will Learn</h2><p>Explore core beliefs and acts of worship that shape a Muslim’s faith and everyday practice. The Five Pillars are a key foundation in this learning path.</p><ul><li>Shahadah — declaration of faith</li><li>Salah — five daily prayers</li><li>Zakat — giving to eligible recipients</li><li>Sawm — fasting in Ramadan</li><li>Hajj — pilgrimage for those able</li></ul><a class="am-pillar-course-link" href="pillars-of-islam.aspx">Explore the Five Pillars <i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-right"></i></a></article></div><div class="col-lg-6"><article class="am-extra-card wow fadeInUp" data-wow-delay="0.08s"><span class="am-extra-index">02</span><h2>Our Structured Curriculum</h2><p>Lessons introduce important areas of Islamic knowledge in a clear, age-aware way.</p><ul><li>Basic beliefs of Islam (Aqeedah)</li><li>Life of Prophet Muhammad ﷺ (Seerah)</li><li>Islamic manners and ethics (Akhlaq)</li><li>Introduction to Fiqh (Islamic rulings)</li><li>Daily Islamic practices and supplications</li><li>Quranic teachings in daily life</li></ul></article></div><div class="col-lg-6"><article class="am-extra-card wow fadeInUp" data-wow-delay="0.16s"><span class="am-extra-index">03</span><h2>Learning Approach</h2><p>Lessons are presented in clear steps and adapted to the learner’s age and current level. Teachers explain key ideas and encourage students to connect their learning with everyday life.</p></article></div><div class="col-lg-6"><article class="am-extra-card wow fadeInUp" data-wow-delay="0.24s"><span class="am-extra-index">04</span><h2>Suitable for All Ages</h2><p>This program is suitable for children, teenagers and adults who want to strengthen their Islamic knowledge and understanding.</p></article></div><div class="col-lg-6"><article class="am-extra-card wow fadeInUp" data-wow-delay="0.00s"><span class="am-extra-index">05</span><h2>Learning Outcomes</h2><p>Students build foundational knowledge of Islamic beliefs, worship and values, with opportunities to discuss how these teachings guide daily life.</p></article></div>
